codex
The comprehension’s semantics allocates two intermediate lists per iteration, which makes the heap invariant unnecessarily noisy. I’m switching to an equivalent supported-subset implementation with one fresh result list and in-place `append`; the unbounded proof can then track one heap cell exactly while still executing every lookup, addition, method dispatch, mutation, loop step, and return.
apply patch
